From: PhantoWD EX4 contributors
Subject: [RESEARCH ONLY] target/iscsi: optionally require configured mutual CHAP

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 PhantoWD EX4 contributors

Keep the upstream default. In the opt-in disposable research profile only,
reject a missing initiator challenge when target credentials are configured.
This is login-time enforcement, not client verification, transport encryption,
credential ownership or revocation of an already authenticated session.

--- a/drivers/target/iscsi/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/target/iscsi/Kconfig
@@ -12,4 +12,15 @@ config ISCSI_TARGET
 	include iSCSI, Fibre Channel and the SCSI RDMA Protocol (SRP).
 	Configuration of the SCSI target mode stack happens through configfs.
 
+config ISCSI_TARGET_STRICT_MUTUAL_CHAP
+	bool "Require mutual CHAP when target credentials are configured"
+	depends on ISCSI_TARGET
+	default n
+	help
+	  Reject CHAP login without an initiator challenge when outbound target
+	  credentials are configured. Without this option, configured outbound
+	  credentials still allow an initiator to use one-way authentication.
+	  This changes only new CHAP authentication, not existing sessions or
+	  transport confidentiality. The default preserves upstream behavior.
+
 source	"drivers/target/iscsi/cxgbit/Kconfig"
--- a/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_auth.c
+++ b/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_auth.c
@@ -426,6 +426,8 @@ static int chap_server_compute_hash(
 	ret = extract_param(nr_in_ptr, "CHAP_I", 10, identifier, &type);
 	if (ret == -ENOENT) {
 		pr_debug("Could not find CHAP_I. Initiator uses One way authentication.\n");
+		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ISCSI_TARGET_STRICT_MUTUAL_CHAP))
+			goto out;
 		auth_ret = 0;
 		goto out;
 	}
